{
  "schema": "runtime-config-conformance/v1",
  "note": "The shared truth table for resolveConfig (issue #1251). Each case gives the runtime-config/v1 or explicitly tagged runtime-config/v2 members that are data as `config` (an object, serialized compactly) or `configText` (raw, for malformed input), the exact `ruleset` and `actionPolicy` text a binding receives as bytes, whether a callback policy is present, and the expected resolution on the artifacts named in `profiles`. A case marked `rawOnly` is text no JavaScript object can produce (malformed JSON, a repeated member), so only the binding-level run, which passes the text through, executes it. `codes` and `paths` list every diagnostic in order (errors first). The Rust core and every JavaScript runtime that loads a binding run these cases against the artifact manifest they report; no surface keeps its own copy of the table. No case carries a scan input or a secret-shaped value.",
  "cases": [
